## Commands

Agents read this table instead of discovering commands. Keep it exact.

| Purpose | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Install | `npm ci` |
| Focused test | `npx jest <path>` |
| Module suite | `npm test -- <module>` |
| Full suite | `npm test` |
| Integration / e2e | `npm run test:e2e` |
| Lint | `npm run lint` |
| Typecheck | `npx tsc --noEmit` |
| Build | `npm run build` |
| Generate migration | `npm run migration:generate -- src/database/migrations/<Name>` |
| Run / revert migration (local only) | `npm run migration:run` / `npm run migration:revert` |

## Structure

- Feature modules live in `src/modules/<feature>/` — controller, service, DTOs, entity, tests.
- Migrations live in `<path>`.
- Shared guards, decorators, filters, and interceptors live in `<path>`.

## Conventions

- Auth: global `<GuardName>`; public routes use `@Public()`. Caller identity from `<@CurrentUser() / request.user>`.
- Tenant scope: every owned table has `<company_id>`; services take it as a required parameter.
- Pagination: `<PaginationQueryDto>` in, `<PaginatedResponse<T>>` out, `limit` max <100>.
- Errors: `<ExceptionFilterName>` returns `<shape>`.
- Cache keys: `<entity>:<scope>:<id>`; invalidate after commit.

## Working Rules

- **Routing:** before backend work, classify the request — new feature, bug, schema change, new endpoint, refactor, tests, review, contract, or question only — state it in one line, then invoke the matching kit command through the Skill tool (`new-feature`, `bug-fix`, `migration`, `generate-api`, `refactoring`, `test-generation`, `code-review`, `db-review`, `api-contract`). If the request could go either way — for example "analyze and investigate" that may end in a change — ask through AskUserQuestion: analysis only, or analysis then the matching command. A question or analysis with no code change needs no workflow.
- **Code exploration:** when `.codegraph/` exists, call `codegraph_explore` (MCP tool, or `codegraph explore "<symbols or question>"` on the shell) **before** Grep, Glob, or Read. Source it returns counts as read — do not re-open those files. Use `codegraph callers/impact <symbol>` for usages instead of grepping.
- **Asking the user:** when you need a decision from the user — in a kit command or in plain chat — ask through the AskUserQuestion tool, one question per call, with the recommended option first and marked "(Recommended)". Never end a reply with a text list of open questions. Non-blocking questions become stated assumptions instead.

## Docs

- API contracts: `<path or link>`
- Feature specs: `docs/backend/specs/`
- Change records: `docs/backend/changes/`

## Process Precedence

When a backend-kit command (`/new-feature`, `/bug-fix`, `/generate-api`, `/refactoring`, `/migration`) is running, it is the process for that task:

- Its `backend-clarify-and-approve` skill replaces `superpowers:brainstorming`.
- Do not run `superpowers:writing-plans` or `superpowers:subagent-driven-development` on top of it.
- Test-first rules come from the `nestjs-testing` skill.

Outside kit commands, superpowers skills apply as usual.
